# Fault injection, testing=AssumeCalleesRetainNothing: Link reports that keep() only calls its arguments, so a caller may allocate the closure in its own frame.
# Together with testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime, the fault is left for the run-time check to catch. Without that switch, the compiler's own checks fail at the store.
# The closure has no name of its own, so it is one that may be borrowed.
# OPTIONS: testing=AssumeCalleesRetainNothing
# DIAGNOSTIC: OpcodeNotInForm 1
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
